Z||000000||MickeyAsh||06-26-2001||12:03 AM||||Well gang, looks like it's time once again for a visit to the forum... as of 3 days ago, my speedo started acting screwy... here's the rundown:<P>1) Speedo seems accurate up to 20mph<BR>2) at 20mph, it jumps to 40<BR>3) it wont pass 60mph... i can be going what I know to be near 80, and it still sticks on 60<P>I've taken the plexi off my instr panel, with the car in park, and moved the needle up, it resists, and when I release, it pops back down to 0, cleaned the connector for the speedo to no avail... any ideas? TIA<BR>-Sheep||||reg||9
Z||000001||fieroluke||06-26-2001||08:59 AM||||One of the coil drivers or one of the coils is bad. There are two coils in the gauge assembly, with their magnetic forces adding up, pointing the needle in a certain direction. If one coil is too weak, the other coil is dominant, and will point the needle in "its" direction.<P>It's difficult to explain, there's an article about the speedo operation on my website (www.fieros.de), but in short: you can try to clean the contacts between coil and board, but other than that, you probably need a new speedo.<P>Best regards,<P>-Oliver<P>------------------<BR>Visit my website: <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  for lots of technical and other Fiero related information<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieros.de/jpg/mycars.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MickeyAsh||06-26-2001||11:16 AM||||I forgot to add the part about me just replacing the speedo... lol... it acts exactly the same as the old one. And I mean exactly. I thought it might be that the old one was just getting hung up or something, but it's exactly the same with the new one.||||reg||1
